WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.280
The mayor, he made it [evacuating] mandatory.

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:05.360
Other than that, I wouldn't have left.

3
00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:10.600
Because I've been through hurricanes and storms.

4
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.640
In fact, we usually have parties, hurricane parties.

5
00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:17.460
You know, because there's nothing to it.

6
00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:18.780
Katrina changed all that.

7
00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:20.360
Yes it did.

8
00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:21.640
Where did you live?

9
00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:22.820
Where were you living?

10
00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:25.740
On Claiborne Street, in the Lower Ninth . . . Ninth Ward.

11
00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:31.460
And after the hurricane, I don't have pictures of any of my children now.

12
00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:32.693
Don't have my children, don't have their pictures.

13
00:00:32.693 --> 00:00:36.000
They're gone, the pictures are gone, the memories . . . I still have the memories.

14
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:42.160
But nothing tangible.

15
00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.140
So I'm here [in New Roads, Louisiana] trying to start over again.

16
00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:46.820
At sixty-seven.

17
00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:49.800
Because there was a time I gived up.

18
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:53.260
I mean, like I said, everybody was dead around me.

19
00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:56.980
I didn't know where my friends were.

20
00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:59.340
I didn't know where my grandchildren were.

21
00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:01.600
I didn't know anything.

22
00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:08.720
I couldn't get a place . . . Even out here, there's some people that was kind of discriminating against me.

23
00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:12.200
But I couldn't find a place to rent, man.

24
00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.140
Wouldn't accept my dog.

25
00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:22.480
But, like I said, when I got on low, not energy, I guess it was energy, but I was about ready to give up.

26
00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:26.760
They was right there, "No, Mr. Cusher.

27
00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:29.620
No, no. There you go."

28
00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:33.140
Those two angels [Cusher and Jewell laugh].

29
00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:35.220
They don't like me to talk about them but I got to.

30
00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:39.760
I told you they gave me . . . they collected $27,000?

31
00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:41.540
Yes, for your new home.

32
00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:43.680
They're part of my survival, you know.
